{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/335704-orpheus-physical-damage-with-wail","id":335704,"title":"Orpheus: Physical Damage with 'Wail'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-09T19:40:17-08:00","id":335704,"title":"Orpheus: Physical Damage with 'Wail'","content":"Does anyone know what the dice pool is for doing physical damage with Wail? The book mentions Vitality costs but not how the damage is accrued or applied.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I'm having trouble finding a ruling on this- Can Projectors use their Horrors when in their bodies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","user":"shkspr1048","date":". 12-11-2014, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T02:26:59-08:00","id":338909,"title":"","content":"I use Manipulation + Empathy vs 6, since most of the horrors tend to have only one or two rolls associated with them so went with one for Wail as a whole but I could see why one could choose other roll, same thing with the difficulty I had a hard time to choose betwenn willpower and a flat 6 but ended with the latter for simplicity sake in case of multiple opponent (do one roll at diff 4, 6 and 7 is kind of cumbersome). In the errata it is written that the soak roll vs Wail is at (Vitality spend + 3) diff.<br /> One other question is since 4+ mention lethal damage is it bashing at 2 and 3, I ruled with the errata which mention lethal at 2+.<br /> <br /> I confess this one of those Horrors that could benefit from some rewritting to clarify a few things.<br /> And that's one of the reasons my Orpheus chronicle has ground to a standstill I need to work out all of those kinks to be able to run the game smoothly (I hate having to rule things on the spot in a middle of a fight) and haven't found the courage to get to it.<br /> <br /> Projectors can never use Horrors while in their bodies (this one is written in ink somewhere in the book), the errata mention one caveat where a Banshee can have uncontrolled vision with Forebode (ie a tool at the st disposal).<br /> <br /> Sorry I couldn't be more helpfull.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4065-foebk","name":"Foebk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T16:21:41-08:00","id":339533,"title":"","content":"Where can I find the errata?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:27:34-08:00","id":340191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/projectorpheus/rules/orpheus_errata.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/projectorpheus/orpheuslogo.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/projectorpheus/rules/orpheus_errata.html\" target=\"_blank\"> New Lament: Risen </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"ht